{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 74,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Maschil of Asaph. O God, why hast thou cast ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "us",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " off for ever? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "why",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " doth thy anger smoke against the sheep of thy pasture?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remember thy congregation, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou hast purchased of old: the rod of thy inheritance, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou hast redeemed; this mount Zion, in which thou hast dwelt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lift up thy feet to the perpetual desolations; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the enemy hath done wickedly in the sanctuary.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy enemies roar in the midst of thy congregations; they set up their ensigns ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " signs.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " was famous according as he had lifted up axes upon the thick trees.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But now they break down the carved work of it at once with axes and hammers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have cast fire into thy sanctuary, they have defiled ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "by casting down",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the dwelling-place of thy name to the ground.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They said in their hearts, Let us destroy them together: they have burned up all the synagogues of God in the land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We see not our signs: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no more any prophet: neither ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " among us any that knoweth how long.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O God, how long shall the adversary reproach? shall the enemy blaspheme thy name for ever?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why withdrawest thou thy hand, even thy right hand? pluck ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " out of thy bosom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my King of old, working salvation in the midst of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou didst divide the sea by thy strength: thou didst break the heads of the dragons in the waters.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou didst break the head of leviathan in pieces, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " didst give him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " food to the people inhabiting the wilderness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou didst cleave the fountain and the flood: thou didst dry up mighty rivers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The day ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thine, the night also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thine: thou hast prepared the light and the sun.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast set all the borders of the earth: thou hast made summer and winter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remember this, the enemy hath reproached, O LORD, and the foolish people have blasphemed thy name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O deliver not the soul of thy turtle dove to the multitude ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the wicked",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": forget not the congregation of thy poor for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Have respect to the covenant: for the dark places of the earth are full of the habitations of cruelty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O let not the oppressed return ashamed: let the poor and needy praise thy name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Arise, O God, plead thy own cause: remember how the foolish man reproacheth thee daily.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.74.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Forget not the voice of thy enemies: the tumult of those that rise against thee increaseth continually.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
